---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="About | Ravikumar Buragapu"
			description="Ravikumar Buragapu is an engineering leader focused on AI engineering, agentic systems, platform engineering, and building reliable, secure, production-ready enterprise platforms."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>About</h1>

			{/* Headshot: add a photo to the project's public folder (for example
			    public/ravikumar.jpg), then remove the comment markers around this line.
			<img class="headshot" src="/ravikumar.jpg" alt="Ravikumar Buragapu" width="160" height="160" />
			*/}

			<p>
				I'm a Director of Engineering with more than 25 years of experience
				building enterprise software and leading engineering organizations.
				Today I focus on AI engineering, platform engineering, and
				reliability at enterprise scale. My work centers on turning emerging
				technologies—from GenAI to agentic systems—into production-ready
				platforms that are secure, observable, resilient, and built to
				operate at scale.
			</p>

			<p>
				I believe the next phase of AI will be defined not just by what models
				can do, but by how well we engineer the systems around them:
				identity, evaluation, permissions, infrastructure, operational
				controls, and human accountability.
			</p>

			<p>
				Across my career, one principle has held: successful technology
				transformation takes more than good architecture. It takes strong
				engineering fundamentals, effective organizations, operational
				discipline, and measurable outcomes.
			</p>

			<h2 id="work">What I work on</h2>
			<p>
				My focus spans AI infrastructure, agentic architectures, LLM
				inference, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), cloud platforms,
				site reliability engineering (SRE), and operational intelligence.
				I work at the intersection of architecture, engineering execution,
				and operations—with an emphasis on making complex systems reliable,
				secure, and measurable in production.
			</p>

			<h2 id="arc">Engineering leadership and impact</h2>
			<ul class="arc">
				<li>
					<strong>Oracle Health</strong>
					<p>
						I lead engineering across infrastructure, reliability, and
						data intelligence platforms spanning commercial, regulated,
						and Federal environments, modernizing them into AI-native,
						action-driven platforms with the operational foundations
						required for secure, highly available, data-intensive
						services. My focus includes platform scalability, operational
						resilience, engineering effectiveness, and the responsible
						use of AI on enterprise engineering problems.
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Wells Fargo</strong>
					<p>
						I formed the Agentic and GenAI Squad, headed the AI-native
						SDLC transformation, and helped define the architecture and
						strategy for agentic workflows across engineering, reaching
						more than 10,000 developers. The work explored how agentic
						AI, developer platforms, and engineering automation can
						improve software development workflows while meeting
						enterprise security and governance requirements.
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Adobe</strong>
					<p>
						I led platform engineering and the Agentic AI Builders Group,
						and built an AI-driven Service Maturity Insights platform that
						connects engineering data to platform improvement. My work
						there included an AI-native developer platform with a modern,
						action-driven CI/CD approach.
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Kohl's</strong>
					<p>
						I worked on AI initiatives and the development of a data
						science engineering platform.
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Earlier</strong>
					<p>
						Engineering roles at Charles Schwab, after beginning my
						software engineering career in India in 2000.
					</p>
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 id="expertise">Areas of expertise</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>AI and agentic systems.</strong> Agent architectures, LLM
					evaluation, retrieval-augmented generation, multi-agent
					orchestration, AI governance, and production AI engineering.
				</li>
<li>
	<strong>Platform engineering and cloud infrastructure.</strong> {' '}
	 Internal developer platforms, cloud-native infrastructure,
	developer experience, automation, and distributed systems.
</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Reliability and operations.</strong> Site reliability
					engineering, observability, resilience, service maturity, and
					operational automation.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Engineering leadership.</strong> Engineering strategy,
					organizational transformation, developer productivity, and
					building high-performing teams.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 id="perspective">Technical perspective</h2>
			<p>
				I’m particularly interested in the engineering principles that
				make AI systems trustworthy and operationally sustainable:
				explicit agent identity, least-privilege access, policy-as-code,
				reproducible evaluation, observability, controlled autonomy,
				and reliable failure recovery.
			</p>

			<p>
				I also care about the broader engineering system—developer
				experience, platform abstractions, automation, and operational
				practices that help teams deliver software faster without
				compromising reliability or security.
			</p>

			<h2 id="convictions">How I think</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>Autonomy should be earned.</strong> An agent's freedom to
					act should rise and fall with measured evidence of reliability,
					explicit permissions, and operational safeguards, not with
					enthusiasm. It is an engineering decision, not a model capability.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Evaluation is the control plane.</strong> The same system
					that measures an agent should decide what it is allowed to do.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Reliability is a design principle.</strong> Observability,
					resilience, security, and accountability belong in the
					architecture from the start, and they matter more as AI systems
					move from producing information to taking actions. Identity,
					error budgets, and rollback are old platform disciplines applied
					to systems that can now act.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Platforms should enable, not constrain.</strong> Good
					platforms reduce cognitive load, offer self-service, and give
					teams secure, reusable foundations so they can focus on delivering
					value.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Leadership builds capability.</strong> The goal isn't only
					to deliver projects. It is to build engineering organizations that
					can adapt, innovate, and execute consistently.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 id="research">Research and continuous learning</h2>
			<p>
				I keep a strong interest in the foundations of AI and in the
				engineering problems of bringing AI systems into production. My
				interests include machine learning, language models, retrieval
				systems, evaluation methods, and agent architectures. Through
				independent projects and continued study, I explore how ideas
				become working systems.
			</p>

			<h2 id="education">Education and credentials</h2>

			<section class="education-credentials">
				<h3>Education</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>
						Incoming Ph.D. Student in Artificial Intelligence
					</li>
					<li>
						Executive MBA — Quantic School of Business and Technology
					</li>
					<li>
						M.Sc. in Physics (Electronics specialization) — Andhra University
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h3>Professional certifications</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>Google Cloud Professional Cloud Architect</li>
					<li>AWS Certified Solutions Architect – Professional</li>
					<li>Certified Cloud Security Professional (CCSP)</li>
					<li>ITIL Master</li>
					<li>IAPP Artificial Intelligence Governance Professional (AIGP)</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<h2 id="more">Speaking, writing, and projects</h2>
			<p>
				I have spoken at DPE Summit, Percona Community Live, and
				ScyllaDB Summit, as well as AI and machine learning panels
				in Santa Clara. My writing explores developer productivity,
				platform engineering, AI governance, and the architectural
				and operational challenges of running AI agents in production.
				My open-source projects focus on measuring and controlling AI
				systems in practice.
			</p>

			<p>
				<a href="/speak">Speaking</a>
				·
				<a href="/writing">Writing</a>
				·
				<a href="/projects">Projects</a>
			</p>

			<p>
				To get in touch, message me on{' '}
				<a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ravikumar-buragapu" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>.
				{/* When your domain email is ready, add:
				   You can also email <a href="mailto:contact@ravikumarburagapu.com">contact@ravikumarburagapu.com</a>. */}
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
